invariant: INV-16
file: aead.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: aead_seal_cpu runs its keystream through chacha20_xor, which takes no
  description of the CPU, so no record or packet a session seals runs the
  AVX2 kernel, whatever CH_CPU_AVX2 says. The bytes are the same.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into each kernel under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds it for x86-64 and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    chacha20_xor_cpu(cpu, key, nonce, 1, pt, ct, n);
    mac(widemul_of_cpu(cpu), key, nonce, aad, aad_len, ct, n, tag);
--- new
    chacha20_xor(key, nonce, 1, pt, ct, n);
    mac(widemul_of_cpu(cpu), key, nonce, aad, aad_len, ct, n, tag);
